FAQs

Is delivery-day PPF possible? 
Yes, when the installer is free and the car is clean. Many owners book ahead of pickup.

Is there a curing wait for new paint? 
No, factory paint is already cured. Most studios apply the film in the first one to two weeks.

Will new paint need correction? 
Often just a light polish. Transport and storage can leave tiny marks.

Does PPF pay off on a new car? 
Yes, it stops chips, scratches, and stains for years. It also helps protect resale value.

When can I wash after PPF? 
Wait for the cure time your installer gives, usually about a week. Then use pH-neutral shampoo and a soft mitt.
